WEBVTT

00:00:29.413 --> 00:00:32.579
And that advice column has ultimately
been adapted into

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:35.246
a New York Times podcast
called Sugar Calling.

00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:41.037
I'm joined by Cheryl Strayed, who is
recording herself in her home in Portland,

00:00:41.037 --> 00:00:44.954
Oregon. Cheryl Strayed, welcome
to Design Matters.

00:00:45.371 --> 00:00:48.454
Hi, Debbie. I am so thrilled to be here.

00:00:48.496 --> 00:00:52.496
I'm a fan of the podcast and I've been
dying to talk to you for ages.

00:00:52.537 --> 00:00:54.496
Oh, I'm so glad. I'm so excited.

00:00:54.912 --> 00:00:59.746
I listen to a recent podcast where you
said that this pandemic has made it clear

00:00:59.746 --> 00:01:04.454
to you that the first thing you are is a
writer. Was that ever really in doubt?